`check-spec-anchor-names.mjs --fix` repoints each citation's line from the test NAME it carries. That's exactly the tool for my situation: the anchor name (test title) is authoritative, and the line is derived. So my workflow:

1. Edit the two test files (dedupe) — keeping test titles unchanged.
2. Add the new anchor to the config-hooks spec with the right name and my best-guess line (or even a wrong line — the --fix repairs lines from names).
3. Run `node scripts/check-spec-anchor-names.mjs --fix` to repoint ALL anchors by name.
4. Run `node scripts/check-spec-anchor-names.mjs` (no flag) to verify zero findings.

